| R-stmt-call | skip-check | stmt-form emits unresolved `macro_expand(...)` C/IR |
| R-user-fn | skip-check | emit-c will emit a user `fn macro_expand` if check is skipped |
| R-not-sink | SECRET | residual names are **not** SECRETSINK |
| R-bc-secret | smoke | `emit-bc` skips SECRET + residual |
| R-fixture | rails | no `residual_ast_macro_fail.oo` |
| R-product-cli | env | `bin/ooda check` → `ERR_NO_PRODUCT_SCRIPT` here; proved via `oodac` |
| R-c-pp | honesty | do not call emit/runtime `#define`s AST macros |

If `AST_MACROS` is ever implemented, 2.8 **reopens**: second-pass SECRET
on **expanded** toks/AST (see `MACRO_SECRET_RESIDUAL.oot`).

========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

**SPRINT 2.8 (runtime auditor): PASS.**

Q1. Does emit/runtime expand macros? **No.**
Q2. Residual refuse names? **`macro_expand`**, **`ast_macro`** (`AST_MACROS`).

